  "text": "The term Celtic Twilight refers to an Irish cultural wave from the early 1900s. It centered on writing, yet it also engaged artists, politicians, and other thinkers. They pictured themselves in a long, shadowed evening that followed a brilliant past age of Celtic strength. Yeats drew on old gods and their legends for his verse. Lady Gregory placed her dramas in a blended, idealized Celtic Ireland. Some of the era's art looks forced next to early modernism. The movement saved much folklore and spoken tradition. It also worked to revive the fading Irish tongue. Those efforts helped make Irish the official speech of the new republic. Schools soon required the language. The movement was based around Míde.",
